> Some questions:
> 1. I've enjoyed using Fire Brand, but is this a good weapon in Hell?
> Do I need to get myself another artifact weapon, and what are the
> chances of that actually happening?  If FB is good enough, I'll use
> all my ?EA on it.  Should I be twoweaponing?

Wizards can't actually twoweapon, so this isn't an issue.  Magicbane is a
much better weapon than Fire Brand for a wizard, as you can become skilled
in dagger.  If you haven't enhanced your skills yet, I would do so now. A
wizard should really also have some good attack spells.  Finger of Death is
great, but uses up a lot of power. Magic Missile is the best in my opinion,
as it does much more damage than Force Bolt, and it doesn't destroy potions.
If you have a wand of polymorph I would polymorph some of the less useful
spellbooks (restore ability, haste self) to get some good ones

> 2. Should I use a wish on a robe? I lost my CoMR to a polymorph
> accident (but it was fun being a dragon for a while!), but I assume
> with EotA and MB I can do without it. On the other hand, the elven
> cloak gives me stealth, which is nice.

See above. I would wish on a new CoMR.  Its indispensible.

> 3. How can I get my spell fail rates down, in particular FoD?  My
> attack spell level is currently skilled, will going to expert do it?

It should do.  Practice makes perfect, after all. I don't think you can get
to expert in all spells though. Don't waste your skill slots on spells you
probably wont use.  I find matter spells are usually useless, except for
very specific instances.

> 4. Does EotA work in Gehennom?  How about after I have the Amulet of
> Yendor?

Yes, it does.  However,  the AoY does strange things to mana regeneration.
After you have the AoY you wont be able to use too many spells.

> 5. Am I ready for the Castle?  How about for Gehennom?  I was thinking
> I could use a \oD, =oC, maybe more attack spells?  Are my HP
> sufficient? What equipment can I safely leave behind?

I would say you should get a CoMR before the castle.  Also, a T-Shirt or
Hawaiin shirt enchanted up to +4 or +5 is very useful to lower your AC even
more.  With Finger of Death a \oD is kind of useless, especially if you have
attack spells at expert.  Most importantly, you shouldn't be burdened.  Try
to identify all your stuff - maybe you can wish up a spellbook of identify,
or polymorph one of your others and hope for the best.  Then throw away
anything useless.  Used up wands, useless wands (secret door detection,
nothing, speed monster), duplicates of rings or amulets. Also, a spellbook
of light would be nice - Gehennom is a dark place. Otherwise, you seem to be
well prepared.

Good Luck!



